tests/error_polymorphic_trait_parameter_must_be_a_type.glos:1:12: Error: The polymorphic parameter of a trait must be a type

    X :: trait($X: s64) {}

    Polymorphic traits are not monomorphized manually. The intended purpose is to know the type of
    the implementer at compile time.

    For example:

        Add :: trait($T: Type) {
            add: (that: T) -> T
        }

        Vec2 :: struct { x, y: f32 }

        add :: (this: Vec2, that: Vec2) -> Vec2 {
            return {this.x + that.x, this.y + that.y}
        }

        addable := Add(Vec2 {69.0, 420.0})

    Here 'T' gets resolved to the type of the implementer, i.e., 'Vec2'.


